     "text": "{\"count\": 0, \"rationale\": \"No single non-foothold, non-target step is a chokepoint. jumpHost:lateralMovement is reachable two independent ways: through memoryDump:credentialAccess (from vpnGateway, supplychain or mailClient) and through vpnSession:authenticate (dmzWeb AND workstation, both reachable from footholds). jumpHost alone reaches the target via codeRepo:collection and mailArchive:collection. Blocking memoryDump leaves the vpnSession route; blocking vpnSession, dmzWeb or workstation leaves the memoryDump route. Blocking jumpHost itself still leaves other routes: backupHost (via dbLogin = containerHost AND memoryDump) reaches the target through vaultRead or codeRepo, and ssoLogin -> appServer -> dbReplica also reaches it. Blocking mailClient leaves memoryDump reachable from vpnGateway or supplychain, so jumpHost is still reached. Every other step lies on only some of these redundant routes.\"}"
